<\/p><p>The consequences of climate change are becoming increasingly _______. <em>(elker\u00fclhetetlen \/ megker\u00fclhetetlen)<\/em><\/p><p>He felt an _______ urge to confess his secret. <em>(ellen\u00e1llhatatlan \/ k\u00e9nyszer\u00edt\u0151)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">elker\u00fclhetetlen \/ kiker\u00fclhetetlen \/ megker\u00fclhetetlen<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): elker\u00fclhet\u0151 \/ kiker\u00fclhet\u0151 \/ megker\u00fclhet\u0151<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 an _______ truth = elker\u00fclhetetlen igazs\u00e1g (pl. The fact that we all age is an inescapable truth.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 an _______ conclusion = elker\u00fclhetetlen k\u00f6vetkeztet\u00e9s (pl. Given the evidence, the jury reached an inescapable conclusion.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ fate = elker\u00fclhetetlen sors (pl. He accepted his inescapable fate with dignity.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 an _______ fact = elker\u00fclhetetlen t\u00e9ny (pl. Death is an inescapable fact of life.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>inescapable<\/strong><\/p><p>adjective: <strong>inescapable<\/strong><\/p><p>adverb: <strong>inescapably<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: inescapable reality \/ inescapable truth \/ inescapable conclusion \/ inescapable fact<\/span><\/p><p>similar: unavoidable \/ inevitable \/ unpreventable \/ certain<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: avoidable \/ preventable \/ escapable<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":null,"study_direction":"front_to_back","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"learning","interval":0,"ease_factor":250,"repetitions":0,"lapses":0,"learning_step":1,"is_leech":false,"introduced_on":"2026-05-19","reviewed_on":"2026-05-26","due_at":"2026-05-26T09:24:30+00:00","previous_state":{"state":"learning","due_at":"2026-05-26T09:12:53+00:00","in