ed \/ full \/ taken<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":null,"study_direction":"front_to_back","color":"#f264ed","review":{"state":"learning","interval":0,"ease_factor":250,"repetitions":0,"lapses":0,"learning_step":1,"is_leech":false,"introduced_on":"2026-05-04","reviewed_on":"2026-05-26","due_at":"2026-05-26T09:16:58+00:00","previous_state":{"state":"learning","due_at":"2026-05-26T09:06:16+00:00","interval":0,"ease_factor":250,"repetitions":0,"lapses":0,"learning_step":0,"is_leech":false,"introduced_on":"2026-05-04","reviewed_on":"2026-05-26"}},"previews":{"again":"1 perc","hard":"15 perc","good":"1 nap","easy":"2 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-06-01T09:05:58+00:00"},{"id":51320,"front":"<p>After years of practice, she became incredibly _______ in playing the piano, effortlessly performing complex pieces. <em>(\u00fcgyes \/ j\u00e1rtas)<\/em><\/p><p>To be truly _______ in a foreign language, one must not only understand grammar but also grasp cultural nuances. <em>(foly\u00e9kony \/ magabiztos)<\/em><\/p><p>The new software engineer is highly _______ in Python and C++, making him a valuable asset to the development team. <em>(szak\u00e9rt\u0151 \/ kompetens)<\/em><\/p><p>Her _______ command of legal terminology impressed the judges during the trial. <em>(mesteri \/ kiv\u00e1l\u00f3)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">j\u00e1rtas \/ \u00fcgyes \/ szak\u00e9rt\u0151<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): \u00fcgyetlen \/ tudatlan \/ hozz\u00e1 nem \u00e9rt\u0151<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ in something = j\u00e1rtas valamiben (pl. He is proficient in several programming languages.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 highly _______ = nagyon j\u00e1rtas (pl. She is highly proficient at public speaking.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 become _______ = j\u00e1rtass\u00e1 v\u00e1lik (pl. With practice, you will become proficient.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ user = j\u00e1rtas felhaszn\u00e1l\u00f3 (pl. The software is designed for proficient users.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>proficient<\/strong><\/p><p>adjective: <strong>proficient<\/strong><\/p><p>adverb: <strong>proficiently<\/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>proficiency<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: proficient in \/ highly proficient \/ become proficient \/ proficient user<\/span><\/p><p>similar: skilled \/ competent \/ expert \/ adept<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: unskilled \/ incompetent \/ inexperienced<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":"proficient\nproficiently\nproficiency","study_direction":"front_to_back","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"learning","interval":0,"ease_factor":250,"repetitions":0,"lapses":0,"learning_step":1,"is_leech":false,"introduced_on":"2026-05-18","reviewed_on":"2026-05-26","due_at":"2026-05-26T09:21:20+00:00","previous_state":{"state":"learning","due_at":"2026-05-26T09:03:59+00:00","interval":0,"ease_factor":250,"repetitions":0,"lapses":0,"learning_step":1,"is_leech":false,"introduced_on":"2026-05-18","reviewed_on":"2026-05-26"}},"previews":{"again":"1 perc","hard":"15 perc","good":"1 nap","easy":"2 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-27T08:55:58+00:00"},{"id":51314,"front":"<p>Everyone was invited to _______ in the celebratory feast. <em>(r\u00e9szt vesz \/ eszik)<\/em><\/p><p>The community members were encouraged to _______ in the decision-making process. <em>(r\u00e9szt vesz \/ kiveszi a r\u00e9sz\u00e9t)<\/em><\/p><p>Researchers often _______ in collaborative projects to share expertise and resources. <em>(k\u00f6zrem\u0171k\u00f6dik \/ r\u00e9szt vesz)<\/em><\/p><p>She chose not to _______ in the gossip, preferring to remain neutral. <em>(r\u00e9szt vesz \/ belekeveredik)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">r\u00e9szt vesz \/ kiveszi a r\u00e9sz\u00e9t \/ osztozik<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4